Design sketch — NOT applied. Gate N2 (ADR-0134, branch n2-design-only)
import integration for the pure-Kotoba K16 kernel: a fifth --source-path for
org-ietf-tcp pinned at d8c15e23b6c169a4ed044cd7764923ecbb789be4 (the same
commit the aiueos :test alias already pins), and the :require lines
native/tcp-stream.kotoba gains. native/rtl8125.kotoba is NOT touched.

Two paths shown because the compiler wants a source root that resolves the
`tcp.seq-core` / `tcp.reassemble-core` namespaces:

  - $AIUEOS_ORG_IETF_TCP_SOURCE_PATH (preferred): an exact checkout, same
    discipline as the four AIUEOS_*_SOURCE_PATH variables; the ADR-2609031030
    reopen procedure says temporary paths must not be assumed to exist, so the
    variable points at a managed checkout whose HEAD the script pins.
  - fallback: the host gitlibs cache
    ~/.gitlibs/libs/io.github.kotoba-lang/org-ietf-tcp/<sha>/kotoba, which is
    where the :test alias materializes the same commit — usable for host-side
    runs where the classpath already holds d8c15e2.

Every hunk below is against aiueos at 0e3523a (N1 tranche one).

--- a/os/aiueos/scripts/build-kotoba-native-kernel.sh
+++ b/os/aiueos/scripts/build-kotoba-native-kernel.sh
@@ (variables, after net_transport_commit=... line 24)
+org_ietf_tcp_source=${AIUEOS_ORG_IETF_TCP_SOURCE_PATH:-"$repo/../org-ietf-tcp/kotoba"}
+org_ietf_tcp_commit=d8c15e23b6c169a4ed044cd7764923ecbb789be4
@@ (commit checks, after require_source_commit net/transport line 47)
+require_source_commit org-ietf/tcp "$org_ietf_tcp_source" "$org_ietf_tcp_commit"
@@ (first compile invocation, --source-path list, line 49-55)
 "$compiler/bin/kotoba-compiler" compile "$source" \
   --source-path "$aiueos" \
   --source-path "$link_frame_source" \
   --source-path "$dma_map_source" \
   --source-path "$mmio_map_source" \
-  --source-path "$net_transport_source" --unpinned \
+  --source-path "$net_transport_source" \
+  --source-path "$org_ietf_tcp_source" --unpinned \
   --target x86_64-aiueos-kernel-v1 --artifact image --fuel 1048576 --output "$kernel"
@@ (second/reproducibility compile invocation, same list, lines 56-62)
   --source-path "$net_transport_source" \
+  --source-path "$org_ietf_tcp_source" --unpinned \
@@ (verify receipt, line 65-70)
 python3 "$aiueos/scripts/verify-kotoba-native-kernel.py" \
   "$kernel" "$source" "$expected" "$receipt" \
   "$link_frame_source/capability/link/frame.kotoba" "$link_frame_commit" \
   "$dma_map_source/capability/dma/map.kotoba" "$dma_map_commit" \
   "$mmio_map_source/capability/mmio/map.kotoba" "$mmio_map_commit" \
   "$net_transport_source/capability/net/transport.kotoba" "$net_transport_commit" \
+  "$org_ietf_tcp_source/tcp/seq_core.kotoba" "$org_ietf_tcp_commit" \
+  "$org_ietf_tcp_source/tcp/reassemble_core.kotoba" "$org_ietf_tcp_commit"
 #
 # NOTE: scripts/verify-kotoba-native-kernel.py hard-codes FOUR capability
 # inputs (line 18: "len(capability_sources) != 4") and a hard-coded module
 # list (lines 105-109). Carrying the sixth pair requires that script to gain
 # two modules in its source_closure list ("tcp.seq-core",
 # "tcp.reassemble-core") and to accept six pairs. That script change belongs
 # to the implementation tranche that first links the objects, together with
 # its own reproducible-receipt re-measurement — the receipt is a committed
 # verdict format, and widening it silently would invalidate the recorded
 # receipts. The build script must not be advanced without it.

--- a/os/aiueos/native/tcp-stream.kotoba   (NEW FILE — the runtime profile module; rtl8125.kotoba untouched)
+++ b/os/aiueos/native/tcp-stream.kotoba
@@ (namespace head)
+(ns native.tcp-stream
+  ;; Gate N2 runtime profile: persistent TCP byte stream for the fixed
+  ;; 4-tuple 10.77.0.10:49155 <-> 10.77.0.1:8443. State machine, RX ring,
+  ;; reassembly, partial send, FIN/RST, bounded retransmit. The diagnostics
+  ;; profile in native/rtl8125.kotoba (tcp-ack-reset-and-receipt) is
+  ;; proof-only and stays untouched; see 90-docs/adr/0134.
+  (:require [capability.link.frame :as link]
+            [capability.dma.map :as dma]
+            [capability.mmio.map :as mapped]
+            [capability.net.transport :as transport]
+            [tcp.seq-core :as seq-core]
+            [tcp.reassemble-core :as reassemble])
+  (:export [stream-status enter-established admit-segment
+            reassembly-admit reassembly-deliver send-stream close-stream]))
+
+;; Deliberately NOT required here: tcp.state-core. amu#611 refuses a module
+;; holding both an i64 shift and a :bool parameter for native targets, and
+;; state-core has both. The state integers (LISTEN 1, SYN_SENT 2,
+;; ESTABLISHED 4, ...) are restated from state_core.kotoba's wire values and
+;; held to the org-ietf-tcp state parity suite as oracle; when amu#611 lifts
+;; the refusal this line becomes (tcp.state-core :as state) and the
+;; restatement is deleted.
+
+;; Deliberately required ONLY for arithmetic that keeps its decisions in
+;; range arithmetic (no shifts): seq-core (wrap, acceptable?, segment-end,
+;; lt?/leq?) and reassemble-core (duplicate?, trim-skip, trimmed-away?,
+;; overlaps?, prefix-len, held-order-key, contiguous?, queue-full?).
+
+;; Status series (ADR-0134 section 6): source integers 97..100 are the
+;; stream states LISTEN 97, SYN_SENT 98, ESTABLISHED 99, CLOSED 100;
+;; rendered NIC_61..NIC_64 / screen STATUS F7..FA. The 90-range is left to
+;; the checksum gates and the existing diagnostics series.
+(def st-listen 97)
+(def st-syn-sent 98)
+(def st-established 99)
+(def st-closed 100)
+
--- a/os/aiueos/native/rtl8125.kotoba
+++ b/os/aiueos/native/rtl8125.kotoba   (NO CHANGE — recorded to make the absence explicit)
@@
